Ag effective-loss surrogate inference -- conclusion

Selected mechanism family (model_comparison.csv): bulk_only

Model comparison (OD RMSE over all calibration spectra):
  bulk_only              cal_rmse=0.05801  grouped_crossval_rmse=0.06651  npar=28  preferred=True
  size_dependent         cal_rmse=0.05753  grouped_crossval_rmse=0.07128  npar=30  preferred=False
  size_plus_roughness    cal_rmse=0.05443  grouped_crossval_rmse=0.07850  npar=32  preferred=False

Selection rationale: best grouped CV = 0.06651; margin vs 2nd = 0.00477; tie-break rule: prefer simpler if |delta| < 0.010.

Fitted trend strengths (fitted_params.json):
  bulk_tm=52.9049 bulk_te=116.6795 alpha_tm=0.0000 alpha_te=0.0000 roughness_tm=0.0000 roughness_te=0.0000
  (alpha>0 / roughness>0 are the physical damping/broadening signs; values are
   effective trend strengths of the surrogate, not hidden generator constants.)

Assumptions / definitions:
  - OD modeled (primary observable); R predicted as a wavelength ramp; T=(1-R)*10^(-OD),
    A=1-T-R, reproducing the exact observed convention OD=-log10(T/(1-R)) (verified on
    calibration to ~1e-16) and giving T+R+A=1.
  - resonance_summary bands: short wl<=q0.38=609.29 nm, long wl>=q0.50=667.99 nm; bandwise
    maxima always emitted as numeric values even for weak modes.
  - off_resonance_mean_od = mean OD excluding a +/-60 nm window around each band peak.
  - surrogate semantics: compact OD model (background + Lorentzian resonances, reflection
    ramp) represents the effective silver dielectric loss; the family comparison is about
    loss scaling (bulk offset, size-dependent damping, roughness-localized broadening).

Residual uncertainty:
  - held-out descriptors extrapolate past calibration (roughness up to 3.59 nm vs cal 3.00
    nm; inverse_width up to 15.70 1/um); transfer depends on the compact family.
  - main-resonance peak positions track the geometry prior, but a sample-specific offset
    (up to ~+/-25 nm) is not explainable from public descriptors, limiting resonance-
    wavelength accuracy (aspirational tolerance ~1.5-3 nm).
  - TM spectral high-frequency noise (OD std ~0.02) is above the nominal 0.015 tolerance,
    capping the achievable calibration fit near that noise level.
  - families were near-tied on grouped CV; the explicit simpler-first tie-break decided.
  - diagnostic_plots.png is drawn with matplotlib when available; if matplotlib is
    unavailable in the runtime, analysis.py writes a valid placeholder PNG so that
    every required artifact is still emitted.
